{"availability":"available","full":"nao1215/gup","name":"gup","description":"Fast manager for Go-installed binaries in $GOBIN: update, export/import, and migrate toolsets across machines","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":612,"forks":28,"created":"2022-02-19T06:31:07Z","updated":"2026-10-08T22:57:18Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://nao1215.github.io/gup/","topics":["cli","command-line-tool","cross-platform","developer-tools","dotfiles","go","go-install","gobin","golang","golang-tools","updater"],"demo":"https://nao1215.github.io/gup/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.218Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.218Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.218Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.218Z","stars":612,"forks":28}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["gup updates and manages the global Go command-line tools in your $GOBIN. go install places each program in $GOBIN ($GOPATH/bin) but never updates it again, keeps no manifest of what it installed, and offers no way to hold a tool at a version you depend on. gup manages that tool set: it brings the whole set up to date in parallel, can pin selected tools to exact versions, and adds the management commands go install lacks: list/check what is installed, remove binaries, export/import the set to reproduce it on another machine, and migrate it to a new $GOBIN. Runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux."],"features":["gup updates binaries in parallel; go-global-update and a go install loop update them one after another. How long each takes to update the same 30 binaries is measured end to end with himorime, and the latest figures,…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nao1215/gup/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"89ecbd75f686facf7c59e0d4d79d21904ab981c7c63230ed649ecb6adab5a308","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.361Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.361Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"wh